# sync-test-staged.ps1.template — STAGED controller of the real F1+F2 sync test (B39/B40). NOT run by the repository. Windows PowerShell 5.1.
# Copy it OUTSIDE the project (e.g. %LOCALAPPDATA%\TwoSidesSyntheticRun\sync-test-staged.ps1). It performs EXACTLY ONE stage per invocation and never advances by itself:
#   .\sync-test-staged.ps1 -Stage A -RunDir <run folder made by build.mjs> -ConfirmPhrase AUTORIZO-ETAPA-A-<first 8 chars of runId> -ExpectedTreeDigest <v4> -ExpectedKeyFingerprint <fp>
# Stages:  A local integrity/environment (no network)      B Atlas read-only baseline (owner types the password in the launcher's hidden prompt)
#          C register + session + ONE batch of ONE operation   D read-only verification, then identical re-send   E receipts/query, final read-only deltas
#          F OUT OF SCOPE of this campaign (refuses)           G safe shutdown/cleanup report; runnable at any time, even after an interruption.
# Protections: stage phrase tied to the runId · fixed order (A<B<C<D<E) · an unfinished/failed stage needs -Resume and the SAME bytes · HTTP only to the allow-list below (no DELETE/PUT/PATCH,
# no other path) · base URL pinned to https://localhost:8443 · only main_v2_* collections are expected and the historical ones must not change · no automatic cleanup of any data · nothing secret is
# printed or written in clear: the synthetic account credential (and the JWT) live only in a DPAPI(CurrentUser) blob inside RunDir, wiped by stage G. The Atlas password is never handled here:
# it is typed by the owner into the hidden prompt of the EXISTING launchers (run-main-inspection.ps1 / run-verify-synthetic.ps1), which this script only invokes.
# Exit codes: 0 ok · 2 invalid parameters · 9 stage F refused · 10 not authorized · 11 prerequisite missing · 12 -Resume required · 13 locked · 20 outcome UNKNOWN (do not create anything new)
#             21 failed · 30 inconsistent receipt/verification · 31 discrepancy against the baseline · 40 stage G found something still active.
